<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — FreeMCP" description="How FreeMCP handles information provided through the website and linked services.">
<article class="container info-page"><div class="eyebrow">FREEMCP / INFORMATION</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="intro">How FreeMCP handles information provided through the website and linked services.</p><div class="info-content"><p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 22 November 2026</p><p>This policy describes the information involved in using FreeMCP. It should be reviewed against actual hosting, analytics, and third-party configurations before production publication.</p><h2>Information you choose to provide</h2><p>When you submit a server, the information you enter may be included in a public GitHub issue and, if approved, in a public registry listing. Do not submit credentials, confidential data, or information you do not have permission to share.</p><h2>Technical information</h2><p>Our hosting and infrastructure providers may process request metadata such as IP addresses, browser information, and access logs to operate and protect the site. Retention and processing depend on the provider configuration.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>Links to GitHub, maintainer websites, and third-party sponsorship or payment platforms take you to services governed by their own privacy policies. FreeMCP may display promotional placements.</p><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>Analytics and cookie practices must reflect the services actually enabled on the deployed website. This draft does not assert that analytics cookies are active or inactive. If optional tracking is introduced, this section and any required consent controls must be updated before activation.</p><h2>Requests and contact</h2><p>For questions or requests concerning registry information, contact <a href="mailto:agents@freemcp.in">agents@freemcp.in</a>. Public GitHub issue content may also be subject to GitHub's own retention and removal policies.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
